"<thinking>\nStep A: Text Breakdown\n- \"mobile football app that will be available for Android and iOS devices.\"\n- \"important...runs quickly and smoothly...fully loaded and ready to use within a maximum of two seconds after starting.\"\n- \"offer football fans a central platform where they can stay comprehensively informed at all times.\"\n- \"users can display current football news of their favorite teams and also select preferred sports channels individually.\"\n- \"users can follow the results of their favorite teams live via a live ticker.\"\n- \"extensive coverage of all leagues and competitions, both national and international.\"\n- \"Detailed team and player information will also be available at any time.\"\n- \"integration of live stream links, for example, from DAZN or Sky Sport. These are available directly in the app as soon as the live broadcast has begun.\"\n- \"that compliance with transmission rights is maintained. Live streams will only be displayed when the respective rights are fulfilled in the country.\"\n- \"option to retrieve the live results of their favorite teams in real time.\"\n- \"integrated live ticker module that enables the retrieval and display of live data in real time.\"\n- \"user interface is designed so that users can access the information in the app directly.\"\n- \"user interface is a key component...connects various modules that are displayed together and managed via the interface.\"\n- \"live ticker module communicates directly via the interface with the user interface to display and continuously update current match data.\"\n- \"live data is retrieved via an API from an external server...provides the data dynamically...module can access it flexibly.\"\n- \"app also offers additional modules that allow users to individually configure the app and connect their own interface to the user interface.\"\n- \"app is linked to a notification system that provides users with information about current events as soon as the notification function is activated.\"\n- \"modules and the user interface are fixed components of the app and remain consistent even with external server updates.\"\n- \"registration and login are designed to be uncomplicated and can be completed directly at app startup.\"\n- \"users have the option to personalize their experience by following favorite clubs and receiving notifications about news or results of their favorite teams.\"\n- \"users can share news and game reports via social media directly from the app.\"\n- \"app...functions reliably even with limited network coverage.\"\n- \"app remains usable offline, even if it temporarily loses connection.\"\n- \"up to 100,000 users can be served simultaneously without performance loss.\"\n- \"app goes through a thorough testing and support process before release to detect and resolve any malfunctions early.\"\n- \"user feedback and app reviews are continuously evaluated to improve functionality.\"\n- \"All personal data of users are processed in compliance with the GDPR.\"\n\nStep B: Requirement Extraction & Sorting\nFR candidates:\n1. Available for Android and iOS devices.\n2. Users can select favorite teams and preferred sports channels for personalized news feed.\n3. Display current football news (filtered by user preference).\n4. Follow results of favorite teams live via live ticker.\n5. Comprehensive coverage of all leagues and competitions, national and international.\n6. Detailed team and player information available.\n7. Integration of live stream links, visible when broadcast begins and rights are met.\n8. Display live streams only if transmission rights fulfilled in country.\n9. Real-time retrieval and display of live results.\n10. Integrated live ticker module updating live data in real time.\n11. User interface connects and manages all modules.\n12. Notification system for events, activated by user.\n13. Registration and login at app launch, uncomplicated.\n14. Users personalize experience (follow clubs, receive news/results notifications).\n15. Users can share news/game reports via social media from app.\n\nNFR candidates:\n1. App runs quickly and smoothly; loaded in ≤ 2 seconds during startup.\n2. App functions reliably with limited network.\n3. App is usable offline, retains functionality after temporary loss of connection.\n4. Must serve 100,000 concurrent users without performance loss.\n5. Interface and modules remain consistent despite external server updates.\n6. App thoroughly tested & supported before release; early fault detection/resolution.\n7. User feedback/reviews evaluated for improvements.\n8. Data privacy: All personal data processed in compliance with GDPR.\n\nStep C: De-duplication & Overlap Check\n- Items 2, 3, and 14 (FR): Merge as one about personalizing news/results by following teams/channels and receiving notifications.\n- Live ticker appears in multiple bullet points; consolidate real-time update, integration, connection to external API.\n- Live stream rights logic: combine availability control (only show with rights for country) with linking system.\n- Platforms (Android/iOS) is environmental, combined as a single NFR.\n- App testing/support and user feedback REVIEW as an NFR about pre-release quality & continuous improvement.\n- Consistency of interface/modules: clarify as resilience to backend changes (NFR).\n- Sharing to social media is distinct and should not be merged.\n- Offline use and degraded network support: two sides of reliability.\n\nStep D: BDD Planning\nPersona: Football fan (casual or dedicated, wants live info and updates). Alternate persona: App administrator (for NFRs). Now draft G-W-T scenario per requirement.\n\nStep E: ID Assignment\nFRs:\nFR-001 (platforms merged to NFR)\nFR-001: Users can follow favorite teams and channels, receive custom news/results (personalization & notification).\nFR-002: Users can access live ticker of matches, with real-time updates for followed teams.\nFR-003: User can access detailed info on any team/player.\nFR-004: User can watch live streams, if link is available and rights for country are met.\nFR-005: User can share news/reports via social media.\nFR-006: Registration/login at startup, must be simple/uncomplicated.\n\nNFRs:\nNFR-001: App available for Android and iOS.\nNFR-002: Startup time max 2 seconds.\nNFR-003: Must support 100,000 concurrent users without performance loss.\nNFR-004: Reliable with poor/no network coverage; usable offline.\nNFR-005: Interface/modules remain consistent despite server/backend updates.\nNFR-006: App is thoroughly tested prior to release; continuous improvement via user feedback.\nNFR-007: Personal data processed GDPR-compliant.\n\n</thinking>"